diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 9fb62ad..2a030a3 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- C++ member calls resolve through the receiver's declared or inferred type, so `fox code Engine.start --rel callers` no longer marks them as guesses by name when several classes have a `start`: a local (`Engine e;`, `Engine e(k);`), a parameter (`Pump* p`, `const Pump& p`), a member of a typed struct (`r.engine.start()`, `s->boat->start()` with a `std::unique_ptr<Boat>` field), `auto e = Engine();`, `auto p = std::make_unique<Pump>();`, `new`, casts, range-for variables and lambda parameters, and the enclosing class's own members (`engine_.start()`, `this->engine_.start()`, a bare `start()`). A receiver whose type can't be told stays a guess. Methods written `void ns::Engine::start()` are indexed. Schema 25; C++ files re-parse once.
+
 - `callers` of a C function-pointer member lists the lines storing a function in it (`.irq_mask = foo_mask,`) as their own group after the call sites, `stores a function in it (not calls): N`, no longer among the references that are not calls, and they no longer make the answer read as incomplete. `callers` of a function counts the documentation lines naming it after the verdict (`plus N in docs (not code, not listed)`) and never lists them.
 - The SubagentStart brief no longer carries the swarm board protocol line by default: in A/B runs it gave parallel subagents nothing and cost more. `[hooks] swarm_board = true` in `config.toml` brings it back. The parent packet and parent read lines stay.
 
